{"step_index":224,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-10T12:21:35Z","input_tokens":5279,"cache_read_tokens":105689,"output_tokens":1410,"content":"### 1. Removed Useless / Duplicate Code\nAll legacy duplicate code and unused UI/helper functions have been cleaned up:\n* **Isolated in [`app_build/`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build)**: All active application code lives exclusively in [`app_build/index.html`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/index.html), [`app_build/styles.css`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/styles.css), [`app_build/engine.js`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/engine.js), [`app_build/explainer.js`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/explainer.js), [`app_build/app.js`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/app.js), [`app_build/engine.py`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/engine.py), and [`app_build/explainer.py`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/explainer.py).\n* **Removed Dead Methods & DOM**: Removed the unused fallback table (`varInspectorTbody`) from [`app_build/index.html`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/index.html) and [`app_build/app.js`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/app.js), removed unused `buildPracticeChallenge` from [`app_build/explainer.js`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/explainer.js), and cleared out the old pre-migration duplicates in the root folder.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Does It Work With Any Type of Python / DSA Code?\n\n**Yes — for any standard Python & Data Structures / Algorithms (DSA) code.**\n\nBecause [`app_build/app.js`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/app.js#L264-L287) now combines the instant in-browser engine ([`app_build/engine.js`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/engine.js)) with an automatic fallback to the real Python `sys.settrace` + `ast` backend ([`app_build/engine.py`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/engine.py)) when running [`server.py`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/server.py):\n\n#### ✅ What Works Out of the Box:\n* **Any Function or LeetCode Class Style**:\n  * Standalone functions (`def binary_search(arr, target):`, `def two_sum(nums, target):`, `def factorial(k):`)\n  * LeetCode classes (`class Solution:` with any method name and type annotations like `nums: list[int] -> int`)\n  * Plain top-level scripts without functions\n* **Auto-Filled Inputs**: If your function expects `arr`, `nums`, `prices`, `target`, `s`, `n`, or `k` and you don't type them in the input box, the engine automatically provides sensible default inputs (and even auto-sorts the list if the function name contains `binary`).\n* **All Core Python & DSA Constructs**:\n  * Variables, multiple/tuple assignments (`left, right = 0, len(arr) - 1`, `a, b = b, a`)\n  * Lists (`nums[i]`, slicing `arr[a:b]`, `.append()`, `.pop()`, `.sort()`, `.reverse()`), dictionaries (`seen[x] = i`), sets, and strings\n  * Loops (`for i in range(...)`, `for i, val in enumerate(nums)`, `for ch in s`, `while left <= right:`) with `break` and `continue`\n  * Conditions (`if / elif / else`), `in` / `not in`, and **short-circuit `and` / `or`** (stops evaluating early when the answer is already known)\n  * Built-ins (`len`, `range`, `min`, `max`, `abs`, `sum`, `enumerate`, `sorted`, `reversed`, `set`, `dict`, `int`, `float`, `str`, `bool`, `round`, `print`)\n  * Recursion (with isolated **Local Scope** frames stacked on top of **Global Scope**)\n\n#### 🔒 Intentional Sandbox Limits (For Safety):\nTo keep execution safe and prevent browser/server freezes, the sandbox intentionally blocks:\n1. **System / File / Network imports**: `import os`, `import sys`, `open(...)`, `eval(...)`, `exec(...)`, `input(...)`\n2. **Async / Generators**: `async / await` and `yield`\n3. **Infinite Loops**: Automatically stops after **400 steps** with a clear `TimeoutError` explanation so an accidental infinite `while` loop never freezes your screen.\n\n---\n\n### How to Run & Test\n```powershell\ncd C:\\Users\\CVT\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\code-flow-visualizer\npython -m unittest test_engine.py -v\npython server.py\n```\nThen open **`http://127.0.0.1:8000`** in your browser."}
